==English==

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|verb}} {{enPR|rĭfŭnd'}}, {{IPA|/rɪˈfʌnd/}}, {{X-SAMPA|/rI"fVnd/}}
* {{audio|en-us-refund-verb.ogg|Audio (US)}}
* {{a|noun}} {{enPR|rē'fŭnd'}}, {{IPA|/ˈriːfʌnd/}}, {{X-SAMPA|/"rI:fVnd/}}
* {{audio|en-us-refund-noun.ogg|Audio (US)}}
* {{rhymes|ʌnd}}

===Etymology===
{{etyl|la}} {{lena}} {{term|refundere}}; prefix {{term|re-}} re- + {{term|fundere}} to pour: compare {{etyl|fr|-}} {{term|refondre}}, {{term|refonder}}. See {{term|fuse}} to melt, and compare {{term|refound}} to cast again, and {{term|refuse}}.

===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

# {{transitive}} To return ([[money]]) to (someone).
#: ''A governor, that had pillaged the people, was {{...}} sentenced to '''refund''' what he had wrongfully taken.'' &mdash; L'Estrange.
#: ''If you find this computer for sale anywhere at a lower price, we'll refund you the difference.''
# {{obsolete}} To [[supply]] again with funds; to [[reimburse]].
# {{obsolete|rare}} To [[pour]] back.
#: ''Were the humours of the eye tinctured with any colour, they would '''refund''' that colour upon the object.'' &mdash; Ray.

